From b1a22bc34242e9744fbdb83c44ac68573b07529f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gitman-101111 <development@spamfolder.xyz>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:23:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] platform: add the reMarkable lpgpr driver

Expose reMarkable's use of the i.MX93 BBNSM general purpose registers
through /sys/devices/platform/lpgpr: the active root partition, the A/B
boot error counters the bootloader honours, boot flow and rescue flags,
and the shutdown state recorded across reboots. Ported from reMarkable's
linux-imx-rm 6.12 tree; the platform-keyring derivation used by the
vendor's dm-crypt swap is left out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
